  "name": "brimstone",
  "_about": "A brimstone (Gonepteryx rhamni), a male 6 cm across the wings: sulphur yellow, a small orange spot in the middle of each wing, the forewing's tip hooked like a leaf's, the hindwing's edge pointed too; beneath leaf-green, veined like a leaf. Six walking legs. Basking, wings spread. Coat: the female (pale greenish white). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/butterflies.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (each wing one sheet, its upperside's painting laid on it as thin sheets in layers -- the 2D butterflies' own paintings, assets/butterflies/; the wings beat in the variant \"flying\").",
